+Polynomial solution-map regularity has a direct predecessor in
+Jeyakumar, Lasserre, Li, and Ph\d{a}m~\cite[Theorem 2.3]{JeyakumarEtAl2016}.
+For a compact polynomial follower feasible set independent of the leader,
+their theorem gives a one-sided inclusion of the nearby solution set
+$Y(x)$ in a H\"older neighborhood of $Y(\bar x)$ at a fixed reference
+leader $\bar x$. Its exponent bound depends on polynomial degree,
+follower dimension, and constraint count. For the structured unique-response
+class here, the following proposition gives a uniform pairwise exponent
+$1/P$, independent of follower count and aggregate degree, with a
+computable rational constant of polynomial encoding length. It also allows
+affine resource right-hand sides that vary with the leader.
